<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/1st-century-bce">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Campaign</p><h1 class="enc-title">Roman expedition against the Garamantes (19 BCE)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">19 BCE</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Roman expedition against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/garamantian-empire">Garamantes</a> was a punitive campaign led in 19 BCE by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lucius-cornelius-balbus">Lucius Cornelius Balbus</a>, the proconsul of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a>, into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fezzan">Fezzan</a> region of the central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sahara">Sahara</a>. According to the Garamantian Empire profile, Balbus captured fifteen Garamantian settlements, including the capital <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/garama">Garama</a>. He was rewarded with a triumph in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>, the last ever granted to a general outside the imperial family.</p></div>
